# 086 · A goal report keeps what it measured; lanes wait while a met champion is confirmed

**Status:** `VERIFIED` · **Version:** [v0.1.0](../../roadmap.md#v010) · **Part:** Running campaigns

## What

1. **A met code-verifier goal keeps its values.** For each goal checked by a kit verifier, the judge keeps the metrics of each public cell's run, met or unmet: in the goal's reasons, in the goal report and its `goal_report` event. The dashboard shows them where the run's goals are listed, in plain text beside the reasons, with no new screen; `get_run` and the REST rig view give them. A metric threshold goal already reports its values: a code goal's values read the same way. Values of public cells may go to the agents (the planner, the workers). A held-out cell's values are never kept or shown anywhere.
2. **Lanes wait while a champion that met every goal is confirmed.** In goal mode, when a validation of the champion has found every required goal met and only the judge's second, confirming validation is left, the scheduler starts no new trial for that run until it is done. A trial already running goes on. If the confirmation does not agree, or fails, trials start again. The run says why, in words, where it says what is at work.
3. **The final champion runs the held-out cells** (the owner, 2026-10-22). The confirming validation also runs the held-out cells of each goal the champion meets, and the run closes only if every one passes. If one fails, the run goes on: the owner sees the cell and its kind, the agents only that the champion was not confirmed and how.

## Why

From a goal campaign that closed on 2026-10-22:

- **A met goal's report had no numbers.** A goal checked by the kit's verifier was reported only as `verifier <name> passed on <cells>`: the metrics each cell's run produced, there a perplexity ratio, were dropped. The owner could not see by how much the goal was met, and the lanes could not see how much room a change had before it lost the goal. A metric threshold goal gave its values; a verifier goal did not.
- **A trial ran after the campaign had, in effect, finished.** A validation of the champion found every required goal met. While the judge's confirming validation was pending, the scheduler started another trial. It ran 50 minutes and used about 139,000 input tokens, and the run's close killed it. Its work could never count.

## Done when

- [x] A code verifier's goal keeps each public cell's metrics, met or unmet: in its reasons, read as a threshold goal's are; as `values` in the goal report and its `goal_report` event; and in the ledger's goal checks.
- [x] A held-out cell's values are kept nowhere: no report, event, goal check, held-out record or agent input.
- [x] The run's **Goals** block shows each goal's reasons, met or not, with its values; `get_run` and `GET /v1/rigs/<rig>/view` give `values`.
- [x] The planner and each worker's brief read the values of public cells.
- [x] In goal mode, while the confirming validation of a champion that met every required goal is queued or running, the scheduler starts no new trial for that run; a trial already running goes on; when the confirmation does not agree or fails, trials start again. **Live** and the run's page say why.
- [x] Tests: values kept for met and unmet code goals; held-out values never in reports, events or agent input; the dashboard shows them; the scheduler holds while the confirmation is pending and goes on after a failed one.
- [x] The pages on goal reports and their event, verdicts, the run's Goals block and when trials start match the code; the changelog has the change.
- [x] The champion's second, confirming validation also runs the held-out cells of each goal it meets; the run closes only if every one passes. When one fails, the run does not close: a held-out record (names and kinds for the owner), a goal report that says by kind alone that the champion was not confirmed, and the lanes go on. A contract with no held-out cells behaves as before.
- [x] Tests: the second validation runs the held-out cells; all pass and the run closes; one fails, the run goes on, the failure recorded with its kind only for the agents, and a change that passes it closes the run; no held-out cells as before; no held-out case's name, values or texts in the goal report, events agents read, briefs, evidence or reasons.

## Decisions

- 2026-10-22, lead, in the build brief: keep each public cell's metrics for a code goal, met or unmet, and show them where the run's goals are listed, in plain text beside the reasons, with no new screen. Never keep or show a held-out cell's values; the held-out pass keeps names and kinds only (goal 082). Values of public cells may go to the agents. While a met champion is confirmed, start no new trial for the run; a trial running goes on; trials start again if the confirmation fails. Say why where the run says what is at work.
- 2026-10-22, builder, within the brief:
  - **Values read as a threshold goal's.** In the reasons, with six significant figures. Met: `verifier <name> passed on <cells>: <cell>: <metric> <value>, …; …`. Unmet: each failed cell and why, as before, then `; measured: ` and the values. The report and its event also carry them as `values`: each cell `{cell, ok, metrics}`, the kit's metrics by name, at most 100 cells. The values are in the reasons so that every reader of a goal report gets them: the Goals block, the planner, the workers' briefs, REST and MCP.
  - **A refused output's values.** A cell whose output the kit's check refused gives the numbers its check reported for the kit's metrics taken from the check (`from: "check"`), so an unmet goal shows by how much. A crash or a timeout gives none. The check is the judge's own program, and the cell is public.
  - **The held-out pass collects no values at all,** so none can leak. Its record keeps names and kinds, as goal 082 decided.
  - **A met goal's reasons are shown.** On the run's **Goals** block a met goal had no line; it now shows its reasons in muted text, a threshold goal's too. Each worker's brief likewise gives a met goal's reasons, so a lane sees how much room a change has before it loses the goal.
  - **What holds the lanes** is a confirming validation (`confirm: true`) queued or running for the current champion. It holds a new round's planning too: a planner call then would be lost the same way. A confirming validation that fails, or does not agree, ends the hold.
  - **Where the run says why.** No place yet says why nothing is at work: that is goal 072. So the scheduler writes a **Live** status line, as it does for its other waits, which the run's **Now** block shows as the planner's line: `no new trial starts: the judge is confirming that champion #<n> meets every required goal; …`, then `trials start again: …` when the hold ends without closing the run. The run's summary line on its page says it too, from control's view (`goals_confirming`, set from the goal report's `confirming`, and cleared by the next report or a failed validation), and so do `get_run` and the REST rig view. **History** says that the judge checks the champion a second time.
  - **A confirmation queued for an earlier champion** is now a first validation of the current one. Before, if a promotion came between a validation that met every goal and its confirmation, the confirmation validated the new champion and could close the run on that one validation. Found while reading how completion is confirmed.
  - **Screens.** The changes are a line in the existing Goals block and a sentence in the run's existing summary line, on the patterns already there, so no mockup was made first.
- 2026-10-22, owner, on the open question of held-out cells on the final champion: "goal 086 yes run held out cells again." The confirming validation of a champion that met every required goal also runs the contract's held-out cells, as an attempt's confirmation does, and the run closes only if the public goals still hold and every held-out cell passes. A held-out failure is recorded as an attempt's is (goal 082: names and kinds for the owner, kinds only for the agents); the goal report says the champion was not confirmed, in fixed words of the kinds; the lanes go on, and the hold ends as after a failed confirmation. A contract with no held-out cells behaves as before.
- 2026-10-22, builder, within the owner's decision:
  - **Which held-out cells.** Those of each goal the second validation finds met; a review goal has none. A goal not met has no claim to confirm, and its held-out cells could only keep a run open that does not depend on it. A goal met long ago is exactly the case the owner's decision closes: an attempt's confirmation runs only the held-out cells of the goals it newly met.
  - **A goal whose held-out check failed is not met.** In the goal report and in the goal tree its status is `unmet`, its reasons `not confirmed: <kinds>; on the measured cells: <its reasons>`. Without this the run could never close: every goal would stay met in the goal tree, so no change could be progress. With it, a change that meets the goal again is screened as progress, and its own confirmation runs that goal's held-out cells.
  - **What the agents learn** is which goal was not confirmed and its kinds of failure, never which cell, how many, its parameters, its output, the check's words or any number from it. The goal is needed for the lanes to work on it, and an attempt's own confirmation already says as much of the goals it newly met; the analysis in goal 082 holds. The owner agreed on 2026-10-22: "This sounds fine". The report adds `not_confirmed`, the kinds in the agents' words over all the goals; the planner reads it, and each worker's brief says it above the goals.
  - **The owner's record.** The `held_out` table keeps a champion's record with its run and champion seq and no attempt: the seed has none, and an attempt's own record must not be read as the champion's (`heldOutFailure`). SQLite cannot drop a column's NOT NULL, so ledger migration 20 rebuilds the table, keeping every row, id and its append-only triggers. The `held_out_checked` event names the run as its subject and adds `champion_seq`; control shows it as `champion_held_out` of the run (`{at, pass, kinds, words, champion_seq}` for the agent token), under the run's goals as **Held-out checks of champion #n**, the attempt page's table, and in History. When no held-out cell ran (the goals met have none), nothing is recorded.
  - **Screens.** One block under the run's existing Goals block, the attempt page's **Held-out checks** table with another title, so no mockup was made first.
- 2026-10-23, lead, after a goal campaign's first validation kept no values: a kit verifier's values are also the numbers its check prints at its top level (at most 24 a case, after the kit's metrics). The kit had declared no metrics, because a metric must be a number above zero in every case's check, and its cases check different things (a ratio in one, a count in another); so its met goals kept only "passed". Held-out cases still keep none. The owner chose to diagnose the unmet goal with these values before workers start ("I'd say option 2 + 1").

## Open questions

- The owner looks at the new lines: a met goal's values in the run's **Goals** block, and the run's summary line while a champion is confirmed (`src/control/goal-report-ui.test.ts` builds both).

